{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"033c9c5e3f475663d5f4a7ac76b5be4b01680534711e2ebdb20ad0c880e6f87b","digest":{"component_or_area":"config module architecture","key_entities":["src/rebar/config.py","src/rebar/_config_writer.py","write_jira_config","_emit_toml","src/rebar/_config_sources.py","src/rebar/_config_schema.py","src/rebar/_config_coercion.py","src/rebar/_config_sections.py","tests/unit/test_config_writer_surface.py","tests/unit/test_jira_onboard.py",".github/module-size-limit.txt","docs/env-vars.md"],"problem_keywords":["module size","code organization","refactoring","config writer","line of code cap"],"propositions":["src/rebar/config.py at 799 lines sits one line under the locked 800-line cap with zero headroom, causing the next line addition to fail CI module-size verification","The config WRITE path (_emit_toml and write_jira_config) forms a closed call cluster that can be cleanly extracted into a new sibling module along the same architectural seam as existing _config_schema.py and _config_sources.py","Extracting the write path preserves public surface: all names previously importable from rebar.config remain importable after re-export, with zero behaviour change for existing consumers","The split reduces config.py from 799 to 658 lines (142 lines headroom below the 800 cap and below the 720 near-cap warning band) while creating _config_writer.py at 196 lines, both within acceptable module-size bounds"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787484253677211001,"uuid":"35a87f43-b003-4529-b369-3ff1be54f77c"}